  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b8a5a27c7b20729498d233b872b276b0, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The parking lot on Rustaveli. Same place I have been for twenty-two
      years.
    midDaysAnswer: Nowhere. The lot is shut down. I walked around for a while.
    finalDaysAnswer: I do not know. I have been walking. It is a habit.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. I have not been to the lot in weeks. My back was
      giving me trouble. It still is.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Work. The lot is open. Everything fine there. Very busy,
      actually. No problems at all.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My daughter's place. She lives close by. Normal visit.
      Nothing unusual.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My knee acts up this time of year. Nothing serious.
    midDaysAnswer: Cannot sleep well. But I never sleep well.
    finalDaysAnswer: Some pressure in my chest. Probably nothing.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. I feel fine. Better than I have in years, honestly.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No. Knee is perfect. Everything is fine. No issues at
      all.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. Sleeping fine. Clear head. No complaints.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Myself. My wife passed four years ago.
    midDaysAnswer: Just me. Got used to it.
    finalDaysAnswer: Nobody. Me and the four walls.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My wife. She is home right now. Keeps the place in order.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My daughter moved back in. Crowded, but it is fine. Better
      than being alone.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Some of the boys from the lot. We share the rent. Practical.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Twenty-two years at that lot and not one car was stolen. Think about that.
    - This line moves slower than the lot on New Year's Eve.
    - You want to see my parking authority badge? I still carry it. Force of habit.
    midDays:
    - The lot is empty now. Strangest thing I have ever seen. Stranger than all of
      this, even.
    - I used to hate quiet shifts. Now I miss them.
    - My wife would have hated all of this. Too much commotion.
    finalDays:
    - Twenty-two years and they close the lot without even telling me.
    - I have a routine. It helps when nothing makes sense anymore.
    - I just stand here. It is what I do.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
